// Split out for #5229: same module as stwwiring.bit (§17.1) — a directory is
// its own Bit module, so Edge, extendEdges and tMacos are already declared or
// imported there and re-declaring any of them here would be E0042.
//
// WHY THIS EXISTS, AND WHY IT IS NOT `assert giveups == 0`. #5228's acceptance
// named a runtime test reading `bit_rt_port_gc_world_resume_giveup` (the
// `giveups=` BIT_GC_STATS field) and asserting it stays 0. #5229's 12-shape
// bound-scan campaign (see that ticket's comments) measured why that can never
// be written: `stwParkBound` (`../../../runtime/gc/gcworld.bit`, 2^32) is
// sized so a legitimately long mark/sweep cannot reach it, and the largest
// shape built — an 18-mutator, 2.5 GB live heap, 4.55-6.65 s genuine
// stop-the-world with every mutator's park within 20 ms of every other —
// still produced 0 give-ups. A scan that shrank the bound to 1/10 and 1/100
// of real produced 103 and 972, so the give-up branch DOES fire; it is a
// wedge detector (`worldRestart` never comes), not a contention counter a
// realistic workload can reach. Asserting 0 on it would pass by construction,
// never by the property holding — the same vacuity this file's header already
// refuses for every other check here.
//
// The deterministic regression for `37f00152` (the fix `#5228`'s stats wiring
// was built to observe) is structural instead: `worldResumeWhenClear`
// (`../../../runtime/gc/gcworldstop.bit`) must still call `worldYield()`
// inside its inner spin, every `stwSpinBurst` checks — `#2415`'s own fix for
// `worldRendezvous`'s identical spin, extended to this one by `37f00152`
// because a pure busy-spin here starves the collector thread it is waiting on
// exactly as a pure busy-spin there starved the mutator `worldRendezvous`
// waits on. `worldYield()` is a one-statement `@nosplit` wrapper around the
// extern `bit_rt_port_gc_world_yield`, and it inlines into its callers (same
// shape as `pollcreatebind.bit`'s `pollCreate`): the relocation this edge
// checks names the extern directly, not the wrapper. `worldResumeWhenClear`
// itself survives as its own atom — unlike `worldYield`, it is well over the
// inliner's size budget (a bounded outer loop around a bounded inner spin) —
// so its atom bounds the search the same way every `Edge{}` in
// `stwwiring.bit` bounds its own.
//
// `path: "runtime/gc"` (not a `darwin`/`linux` subdirectory) because both the
// caller and the wrapper are cross-platform files (`gcworldstop.bit`,
// `gcyield.bit`); `bit_rt_port_gc_world_yield` itself is declared `extern` —
// same seam `gcmark.bit`'s own header documents for
// `bit_rt_gc_mark_stack_overflow` — and stays UNDEFINED in this freestanding
// object regardless of target, so one macOS build is enough to see the edge;
// a second Linux build would exercise the identical cross-platform source.
//
// MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED. `bit build runtime/gc --emit-obj --freestanding
// --target aarch64-macos` (#5229) shows `_worldResumeWhenClear` defined at
// 0x342c, the next symbol (`_bit_rt_port_gc_world_park`) at 0x35ac, and a
// `BR26` relocation to `_bit_rt_port_gc_world_yield` at 0x34e0 — inside that
// span — matching #5195's engineer's by-hand disassembly (`bl
// _bit_rt_port_gc_world_yield` at 0x34e0, gated on `spins % stwSpinBurst`,
// the identical shape `worldRendezvous` compiles to).
const whyResumeYield: string = "worldResumeWhenClear's inner spin must call worldYield() (-> bit_rt_port_gc_world_yield) every stwSpinBurst checks, or a real stop-the-world starves the collector thread precisely as #2415 found for worldRendezvous's identical spin; the give-up counter this fix also wired (#5228) cannot itself be asserted at 0, since #5229's bound scan measured it unreachable by any legitimate workload (stwParkBound sized not to be reached) - see that ticket for the campaign"

// The one edge: `worldResumeWhenClear`'s atom must still reference the yield
// extern. Delete the `worldYield()` call in
// `runtime/gc/gcworldstop.bit`'s `worldResumeWhenClear` -> red.
fn worldResumeYieldEdges(): []Edge {
  return [
    Edge{
      path = "runtime/gc",
      target = tMacos,
      forbid = false,
      fromSym = "worldResumeWhenClear",
      toSym = "bit_rt_port_gc_world_yield",
      why = whyResumeYield,
    },
  ]
}
